<attribute name="refinedDescription" nodeId="6067f719">Functional requirements describe capabilities the system will be able to perform in terms of behaviors or operations -
specific information, application actions, or responses. Functional Requirements specify what the solution or product must
do, and they must be specified in a way that is independent of the technology that will be used to implement the solution.
This approach allows the logical essence of the requirement to be abstracted in a way that enables alternate technical
implementation options to be evaluated later during design without technological bias obfuscating or substituting for the
real requirement.</attribute>
